$DATUM 1-Acety5-(5-phenylpyridin-3-yl)-2,3-dihydro-1 H-indole (22). The title
compound was synthesized according to method A using 17a (150 mg, 0.52
mmol), 3-bromo-5-phenylpyridine (153 mg, 0.63 mmol), sodium carbonate
(277 mg, 2.61 mmol), and tetrakis- (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (30
mg, 0. 03 mmol) in dimethoxyethane (9 mL) and water (3 mL). The crude
product was purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(MeOH/CH2Cl2, 0 to 2%) and crystallization from acetone. Pale yellow
crystals, yield 137 mg, 84%. mp 168 −170 °C. Rf = 0.24 (MeOH/CH2Cl2,
1:20). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.26 (s, 3H), 3.29 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
4.13 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.42 −7.52 (m, 5H), 7.64 (m, 2H), 8.03 (d, J =
2.0 Hz,1H), 8.32 (d, J = 8.3 Hz,1H), 8.79 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl
3): δ 24.2, 28.0, 49.0, 117.4, 123.2, 126.8, 127.2, 128.3, 129.1, 132.2,
132.8, 132.9, 136.5, 136.8, 137.6, 143.3, 146.2, 146.3, 168.8. MS (ESI)
m/z = 315 [M + H]+.
