$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step C: A stirred mixture of
1-((5-bromopyridin-2-yl)oxy)-2-methylpropan-2-ol (25 g, 102 mmol),
4,4,4',4',5,5,5',5'-octamethyl-2,2'-bi(1,3,2-dioxaborolane) (38.7 g, 152
mmol)), PdCl2(dppf)*DCM (24.89 g, 30.5 mmol), and potassium acetate (29.9
g, 305 mmol)) in 1,4-dioxane (339 ml, 102 mmol)) was purged three times
with nitrogen and placed under vacuum three times. The mixture was heated
to 100 °C. After 16 h, the reaction was cooled to room temperature then
concentrated under reduced pressure. The black residue was purified on
silica gel (0-30% ethyl acetate in heptanes).
2-methyl-1-((5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridin-2-yl)oxy)propan-2-ol
as a colorless solid (25 g, 85 mmol, 84 % yield). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 8.38 (1 H, dd, J = 2.0, 0.7 Hz), 7.88 (1 H, dd, J = 8.3, 2.2
Hz), 6.82 (1 H, dd, J = 8.3, 0.7 Hz), 4.62 (1 H, s), 4.07 (2 H, s), 1.30
(12 H, s), 1.17 (12 H, s). Mass Spectrum (pos.) m/e: 294.4 (M+H)+.
