$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A. In an argon-fed glovebox,
zinc bromide (10 mol %: 11.2 mg, 0.05 mmol), IMes (L1 for 20 mol %: 30.4
mg, 0.1 mmol) and MTBE (2 mL) were added to a Schlenk tube equipped with
a magnetic stirring bar. After stirring for 30 min, diboron reagent (0.75
mmol; for B2pin2: 190.4 mg, B2neop2: 169.4 mg) and KOMe (52.6 mg, 0.75
mmol) were added and the reaction was stirred for an additional 30 min.
To this reaction mixture, aryl halide (0.5 mmol) was added. The resulting
reaction mixture was stirred vigorously at rt for the indicated amount of
time. The reaction mixture was then diluted with Et2O (2 mL) and filtered
through a plug of celite (φ 3 mm x 8 mm) with copious washing (Et2O). The
solvents were removed in vacuo, and the residue was purified by flash
chromatography. 2-(Thiophene-2-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethy[1,3,2]dioxaborolane
(18b) [Table 2, entry 18].6,8 Following general procedure A, a white
solid in 84% yield (88.0 mg) from 2-iodothiophene (18a, 105.0 mg, 0.5
mmol). The reaction was complete within 8 h using 10 mol % of catalyst.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.65 (dd, J = 3, 1 Hz, 1H), 7.63 (dd, J = 5, 1
Hz, 1H), 7.19 (dd, J = 5, 3 Hz, 1H), 1.34 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 137.2, 132.5, 128.3, 84.2, 24.9. The carbon directly attached
to the boron atom was not detected, likely due to quadrupolar broadening.
11B NMR (96 MHz, CDCl3): δ 29.0. GC-MS: [t = 8.76 min] m/z 210 (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Synthesis of Aryl Boronates via Zinc-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling
of Alkoxy Diboron Reagents with Aryl Halides at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bose, Shubhankar Kumar; Marder, Todd B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(17), 4562-4565

