$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Palladium-catalyzed borylation of aryl triflate.11 A dry two-necked flask
was charged with KOAc (3 equiv), bis(neopentylglycolato)diboron (1.1
equiv), PdCl2(dppf)·CH2Cl2 (3 mol%), o-silylaryl triflate, and DMSO under
a nitrogen atmosphere. The solution was heated at 80 °C overnight. The
mixture was filtered through a Celite pad using EtOAc as the eluent. The
organic extracts were washed with H2O twice and dried over MgSO4. The
corresponding o-silylphenylboronate ester was obtained after column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc) and bulb-to-bulb distillation.
6-(5,5-Dimethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborinan-2-yl)-1,1-dimethyl-2,3-dipropyl-5-(trimethylsilyl)-1H-benzo[b]silole
(41) This compound is synthesized by the palladium-catalyzed borylation
of the silole 40. The procedure is the same as the borylation of aryl
triflate described in S-9. Colorless oil, yield 84%. Rf 0.30
(Hexane/EtOAc = 50/1). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 399.78 MHz) δ: 0.28 (s, 6H), 0.30
(s, 9H), 0.95 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 0.98 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (s,
6H), 1.47-1.58 (m, 4H), 2.38 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.53 (t, J = 7.6 Hz,
2H), 3.76 (s, 4H), 7.56 (s, 1H), 7.99 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.53
MHz) δ: -3.42, 0.70, 14.4, 14.5, 22.0, 22.1, 23.6, 28.9, 31.7, 32.0,
72.0, 126.9, 137.3, 143.2, 147.8, 150.8, 151.4. IR (ATR): 2956 w, 2930 w,
2893 w, 2871 w, 1713 w, 1577 w, 1499 w, 1476 w, 1415 w, 1378 w, 1344 m,
1284 m, 1243 s 1219 w, 1162 w, 1136 m, 1097 w, 1039 w, 1000 w, 835 s, 768
m, 694 w, 682 w, 657 w. MS, m/z (relative intensity, %): 429 (25), 428
(M+, 68), 427 (17), 414 (18), 413 (51), 412 (12), 399 (18), 385 (21), 357
(21), 329 (10), 327 (20), 315 (10), 313 (10), 272 (11), 271 (39), 269
(19), 257 (14), 243 (10), 143 (12), 133 (11), 75 (17), 69 (40), 59 (26).
Exact mass calcd for C24H41O2Si2B: 428.2738. Found: 428.2740.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
