$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of
5-Bromo-1-methyl-3-[5-(morpholine-4-carbonyl)-pyridin-2-ylamino]-1H-pyridin-2-one
(39.8 g, 101mmol), Bis(pinacolato)diboron (30.7 g, 121mmol), Pd(OAc)2
(0.46g, 2.05 mmol ), X-Phos (1.46 g, 3.06mmol), KOAc (46.0 g, 469mmol),
and dioxane (240 mL) was stirred and degassed three times. The mixture
was heated at 100°C for 2 hours then cooled to 65°C. The slurry was
filtered through a pad of celite (27 g). The cake was washed with 240 ml
of dioxane. The filtrate was distilled under vacuum to 160 ml. The
residue was heated to 65° C. Heptane (240 mL) was slowly added over 1 h.
The slurry was cooled to rt and further cooled in an ice bath for 4
hours. The product was isolated by filtration and washed with a mixed
solution of heptane (100 mL) and dioxane (50 mL) that had been precooled
to 5° C. The cake was dried overnight in a 70°C in vacuum oven. The
product was obtained as a light brown solid (37.5 g, 84% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Based Drug Design of RN486, a Potent and Selective Bruton's
Tyrosine Kinase (BTK) Inhibitor, for the Treatment of Rheumatoid
Arthritis
