$DATUM N-(2-Chlorophenyl)-N-methyl-8-(1H-pyrazol-5-yl)-4,5-dihydrobenzo[b]thieno[2,3-d]oxepine-2-carboxamide
(19). A solution of 47 (200 mg, 0.47 mmol) in MeCN (1.5 mL) and water
(1.5 mL) was treated with 3-pyrazoleboronic acid (65 mg) and potassium
acetate (150 mg). The mixture was purged with nitrogen and then charged
with Pd(PPh3)4 (41 mg). The mixture was heated by microwave irradiation
at 140 °C for 20 min. The mixture was diluted with water and extracted
with ethyl acetate. Purification by reverse phase HPLC gave 19. This
gave. As a colorless solid(194 mg, 83% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO) δ
13.30, 12.93 (br s, 0.2 + 0.8H, pyrazole tautomer NHs), 7.76−7.34
(overlapping m, 8H), 6.73 (s, 1H), 6.59 (br s, 1H), 4.20 (br s, 2H), 3.30
(s, 3H, obstructed by water), 2.97 (br s, 2H). LCMS: (M)+ 436.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rational Design of Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase α Inhibitors That Exhibit
Selectivity over the Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase β Isoform
