$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(5'''''-methyl-3',3'',3''',3'''',3'''''-pentahexyl-2,2':5',2'':5'',2''':5''',2'''':5'''',2'''''-sexithiophene-5-yl)-1-pentyl-1H-1,2,3-triazole
(1). A solution of 23 (0.25 g, 0.40 mmol), 12 (0.30 g, 0.44 mmol) and
K2CO3 (5 mL, 10 mmol) in dimethoxyethane (5 mL) was degassed for 5 min
before Pd(PPh 3) 4 (0.023 g, 0.02 mmol) was added and the suspension
heated to 130 °C by microwave heating for 1 h. The resulting solution was
diluted with n-hexane, washed with H2O before the organic layer was
separated and dried in vacuo. The resulting crude residue was purified
via flash chromatography (SiO2, n-hexane, 20% EtOAc) follows by
recrystallization from ethanol to give 1 (0.35 g, 0.33 mmol, 83% yield)
as a red solid. m.p. 42 - 46 °C; Rf 0.18 (n-hexane, 20% EtOAc); IR (KBr)
3119, 2955, 2925, 2855, 1559, 1506, 1461, 1377, 1223, 1050, 823, 802, 726
cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.70 (s, 1H), 7.36 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.14 (d, J=
4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (s, 1H), 6.99 (s, 1H), 6.97 (s, 1H), 6.89 (s, 1H), 6.62
(s, 1H), 4.41 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H), 2.88 - 2.77 (m, 8H), 2.76 - 2.69 (m,
2H), 2.47 (s, 3H), 1.98 (p, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H), 1.69 (qd, J= 14.5, 7.5 Hz,
10H), 1.51 - 1.27 (m, 34H), 0.98 - 0.88 (m, 18H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
142.6, 140.1, 139.94, 139.85, 139.7, 139.6, 138.0, 135.52, 134.49, 134.0,
133.9, 133.8, 132.7, 130.3, 130.2, 129.7, 128.5, 128.4, 128.14, 128.05,
126.1, 124.3, 118.8, 50.5, 31.7, 30.6, 30.51, 30.49, 30.48, 30.0, 29.44,
29.42, 29.40, 29.37, 29.2, 28.6, 22.6, 22.1, 15.3, 14.1, 13.8; HRMS
(ESI): calcd for for C62H87N332S6 Na [M+Na]+: 1088.5122, found:
1088.5138; elemental analysis calcd (%) for C62H87N3S6: C 69.8, H 8.2, N
3.9, S 18.0; found: C 69.5, H 8.5, N 4.25, S 17.9.
