$DATUM Difluoro[5-[3-hexylthiophen-2-yl]-1-[[5-[3-hexylthiophen-2-yl]-3-(2-methoxyphenyl)-2H-isoindole-1-yl]methylene]-3-(2-methoxyphenyl)-1H-isoindolate-N1,N2]boron
(9). To a solution of 2 (500 mg, 0.755 mmol) and
5,5-dimethyl-2-(3-hexylthiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborinane 8 (423 mg, 1.51
mmol) in THF (25 mL) was added K2CO3 aqueous solution (2M, 7.5 mL) under
a N2 atmosphere. The solution was degassed by two freeze-pump-thaw
cycles. After adding Pd(PPh3)4 (175 mg, 0.151 mmol) to the solution, the
resulting solution was stirred under reflux for 16h under a N2
atmosphere. After cooling, AcOEt (50 mL) and H2O (1 mL) were added to the
solution. The resulting solution was evaporated in vacuo and extracted
with AcOEt (200 mL), and dried with Na2SO4. After the removal of solvent
in vacuo, the residue was chromatographed on silica gel (Wacogel C-300)
using CHCl3 and hexane mixture (3:1 v/v) as an eluent to give dye 9 (420
mg) in 83% yield. 1H NMR (270 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm): 0.76-0.81 (6H, m),
1.13-1.23 (12H, m), 1.43-1.55 (4H, m), 2.59 (4H, t, J= 7.33 Hz), 3.68
(3H, s), 3.74 (3H, s), 6.99-7.23 (6H, m), 7.04 (2H, d, J= 5.10 Hz),
7.40-7.51 (4H, m), 7.47 (2H, d, J= 5.08 Hz), 7.61 (2H, d, J= 9.18 Hz),
8.22 (2H, d, J= 8.29 Hz), 8.73 (1H, s, Ha); FAB MS : m/z 836 [M]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solution degassed by two freeze-pump-thaw cycles prior to addition of Pd
catalyst, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Near-Infrared Absorbing Boron-dibenzopyrromethenes that Serve As
Light-Harvesting Sensitizers for Polymeric Solar Cells
