$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2,4-Diamino-5-(furan-2-yl)-7-(β
-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (8a). An argon-purged
mixture of 2,4-diamino-5-iodo-7-(β-
D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine 2729 (305 mg, 0.75 mmol),
furan-2-boronic acid (126 mg, 1.125 mmol), Na2CO3 (239 mg, 2.25 mmol),
Pd(OAc)2 (8 mg, 0.036 mmol), and TPPTS (53 mg, 0.093 mmol) in water/MeCN
(2:1, 5 mL) was stirred at 100 °C for 3 h. After cooling, the mixture was
neutralized using aq HCl (1 M) and concentrated to dryness in vacuo, and
the residue was purified by reverse phase HPFC (C-18, 0→ 100% MeOH in
water) to afford 8a which was crystallized from water. 2,4-Diamino-7-(β
-D-ribofuranosyl)-5-(thiophen-2-yl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (8c).
Compound 8c was prepared as described for 8a from 27 (305 mg, 0.75 mmol)
and thiophene-2-boronic acid as a white foamy solid (227 mg, 83%). Mp
130-132 °C. [α ]D -57.1 (c 0.273, DMSO). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6): 3.51
(ddd, 1H, Jgem = 11.9 Hz, J5´ a,OH = 5.9 Hz, J5´ a,4´ = 3.8 Hz, H-5´a);
3.59 (ddd, 1H, Jgem = 11.9 Hz, J5´ b,OH = 5.1 Hz, J5´ b,4´ = 3.9 Hz,
H-5´b); 3.84 (btd, 1H, J4´ ,5´a = J4´ ,5´b = 3.8 Hz, J4´ ,3´ = 3.1 Hz,
H-4´); 4.05 (btd, 1H, J3´ ,2´ = J3´,OH = 4.7 Hz, J3´ ,4´ = 3.1 Hz, H-3');
4.35 (td, 1H, J2´ ,1´ = J2´,OH = 6.4, J2´ ,3´ = 5.2 Hz, H-2'); 5.06 (d,
1H, JOH,3´ = 4.4 Hz, OH-3´); 5.16 (bdd, 1H, JOH,5´a = 5.9 Hz, JOH,5´b =
5.2 Hz, OH-5´); 5.27 (d, 1H, JOH,2´ = 6.3 Hz, OH-2´); 5.80 (bs, 2H,
NH2-2); 5.90 (vbs, 2H, NH2-4); 5.96 (d, 1H, J1´,2´ = 6.5 Hz, H-1'); 7.09
(dd, 1H, J3,4 = 3.5 Hz, J3,5 = 1.2 Hz, H-3-thienyl); 7.14 (dd, 1H, J4,5 =
5.2 Hz, J4,3 = 3.5 Hz, H-4-thienyl); 7.15 (s, 1H, H-6); 7.50 (dd, 1H,
