$DATUM 3'-Hexyl-2,2'-bithiophene-5-carbaldehyde (6). A solution of 5 (6.80 g,
35.6 mmol), 4 (10.5 g, 35.6 mmol) and Cs2CO3 (34.8 g, 107 mmol) in
toluene (80 mL) was degassed by bubbling N2 through the solution for 10
min. Pd(PPh3)4 (2.05 g, 1.78 mmol) was added and the resulting solution
was vigourously refluxed overnight under inert atmosphere. The solution
was cooled to room temperature and diluted with n-hexane, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography (SiO2, n-hexane, 5% EtOAc) to give 6 (8.27 g, 29.7 mmol,
83% yield) as a yellow oil. Rf 0.15 (n-hexane, 5% EtOAc); IR (neat) 2954,
2927, 2856, 1665, 1447, 1226, 1056, 836, 804, 754, 728, 669 cm-1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 9.86 (s, 1H), 7.68 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.25 (d, J= 5.0 Hz, 1H),
7.19 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H), 6.95 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 2.85 - 2.73 (m, 2H),
1.70 - 1.57 (m, 2H), 1.42 - 1.20 (m, 6H), 0.86 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 3H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 182.6, 146.6, 142.3, 142.1, 136.7, 130.7, 129.6, 126.2,
125.8, 31.6, 30.4, 29.6, 29.2, 22.6, 14.0; LRMS (EI): m/z (%): 69 (21),
135 (13), 178 (14), 179 (80), 181 (12), 207 (19), 208 (17), 278 (100),
279 (17.5); HRMS (EI): Calcd for C15H18O32S2 [M]+·: 278.0799, found:
278.0791.
