$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Linear [5]pyridine[4]pyrrole 5. A mixture of 2 (1.50 g; 4 mmol), 3 (0.57
g; 1 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (22.4 mg; 0.1 mmol), PPh3 (52.4; 0.2 mmol) mg and
K2CO3 (0.69 g; 5 mmol) was suspended in 30 mL DMF and 6 mL water.6 The
reaction was then heated at 70 °C under N2 for 5 h. After the reaction
mixture was cooled to r.t., the organic layer was extracted with
dichloromethane and washed with water three times. After removal of the
solvent and other volatiles, the reaction mixture was purified by
chromatography over silica gel (hexanes/CH2Cl2, 3/1). This yielded 5 in
the form of a bright yellow solid. Yield: 83%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
= 10.59 (br s, 2 pyrrole NH), 10.44 (br s, 2 pyrrole NH), 7.78-7.72 (t, J
= 10.6 Hz, 1 pyridine CH), 7.46-7.44 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 2 pyridine CH),
