$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Suzuki Coupling Reaction -Synthesis of
Compounds 5 and 7 To a 100 ml two-neck round-bottom flask under nitrogen
atmosphere, the N,N'-bis(2-ethylhexyl)-1,7-dibromoperylene diimide 4
(0.77 g, 1 mmol) and corresponding boronic acid (0.28 g, 2.2 m.mol) were
dissolved in 15 ml tetrahydrofuran (THF). To this reaction mixture 10 ml
of 1 M K2CO3 aqueous solution was added. Catalyst Pd(PPh3)4 (0.058 g,
0.05 mmol) was added and stirred for 24 hours at 80 ⁰C under nitrogen
atmosphere. Reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and
extracted with dichloromethane. The collected organic layer was dried
over anhydrous sodium sulfate. The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. The crude product was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using dichloromethane/hexane (1:1) as eluent.
N,N′-Di(2-ethylhexyl)-1,7-di(thiophen-2-yl)perylene-3,4,9,10-tetracarboxylicaciddiimide
(7)2 Yield 83%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
