$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Alky4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)isoquinolin-1(2H)-one
(I-29). In a 500 mL round-bottomed flask was bis(pinacolato)-diboron
(5.68 g, 22.35 mmol) and I-28 (22.35 mmol), acetic acid, and potassium
acetate (6.58 g, 67.1 mmol) in DMSO (112 mL) to give a darkorange
solution. The reaction was purged with nitrogen gas, and then
Pdcl2(dppf)-CH2Cl2 adduct (1.095 g, 1.341mmol) was added.The reaction was
heated at 80 °C for 18 h and then cooled to room temperature. The
reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc (800 mL) and washed with water
(3x300mL) and saturated NaCl (1x300 mL). The organic layerwas dried
(MgSO4), filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified via Biotage.
2-Isopropy4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-isoquinolin-1(2H)-one
(I-29−1). General procedure F was followed to give I-29−1 from I-28−1 in
83% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.32 (d, J = 7.58 Hz, 1H), 8.26
(dq, J = 0.71, 7.99 Hz, 1H), 7.70 - 7.78 (m, 2H), 7.47 - 7.54 (m, 1H),
5.13 (quin, J = 6.82 Hz, 1H), 1.36 (d, J = 7.07 Hz, 6H), 1.34 (s, 12H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Isoquinolinone Indole Acetic Acids as Antagonists of
Chemoattractant Receptor Homologous Molecule Expressed on Th2 Cells
(CRTH2) for the Treatment of Allergic Inflammatory Diseases
