$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura
Cross-coupling and physical data of the products A two-necked, 25-mL,
round-bottom flask was equipped with a rubber septum, a magnetic stirring
bar, and a reflux condenser to which a nitrogen inlet and an oil bubbler
were attached. The flask charged with aryl chloride (3a-x) (0.5 mmol),
dichloro (1,3-bis(dicyclohexylphosphino)propane) palladium (9.2 mg, 0.015
mmol) and copper iodide (1.9 mg, 0.01 mmol) was flushed with nitrogen.
Tetrabutylammonium 2-pyridyltriolborate salt (2a-e) in DMF solution (0.72
M, 1.74 mL, 1.25 mmol, 2.5 equiv.), N-methylethanolamine (8 μL, 0.01
mmol) and dry DMF (1.25 mL) were added, and the mixture was stirred for
16 h at 100 °C in an oil bath. After cooling to rt, the crude mixture was
extracted with ethyl acetate, washed with saturated NH4Cl, brine and
dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel with hexane/ethyl
acetate. 2-arylpyridine derivatives (4).
3-Methyl-2-(2-pyridinyl)quinoline (4au) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.72
(d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H), 8.13 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (s, 1H), 7.89-7.82
(m, 2H), 7.77 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (ddd, J = 8.5, 6.9, 1.5 Hz, 1H),
7.52 (ddd, J = 8.0, 6.9, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (ddd, J = 7.0, 5.0, 1.8 Hz,
1H), 2.61 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.0, 157.9, 148.5, 146.3,
137.3, 136.7, 130.0, 129.3, 128.6, 127.9, 126.69, 126.67, 124.3, 122.9,
20.3; MS (EI): m/z (%): 219 (100, [M-H]+), 218 (20), 156 (10), 110 (10);
HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C15H11N2 +: 219.0922; found: 219.0916.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
