$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of compound DPIO. To a degassed mixture of dioxane (10 mL) and
H2O (2 mL), was added 7 (350 mg, 1.01 mmol), 4-pyridineboronic acid (309
mg, 2.51 mmol), potassium phosphate (643 mg, 3.03 mmol),
tris(dibenzylideneacetone)-dipalladium (9.2 mg, 0.010 mmol), and
tricyclohexylphosphine (8.5 mg, 0.030 mmol) under Ar atmosphere. The tube
containing the reaction mixtures was sealed with an aluminum crimp cap
fitted with a silicon septum, and subjected to microwave irradiation for
12 h at 130°C. After cooling to room temperature, the reaction mixture
was diluted with H2O (30 mL), extracted with DCM (30 × 3 mL). The
combined organics were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and then
evaporated to dryness. The resulting solid was subjected to silica gel
column chromatography using DCM as eluent. 289 mg (0.838 mmol, 83% yield)
of DPIO as a yellow solid. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for C22H23N3O [M+H]+:
345.1841, found: 345.1849.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, sealed tube used, Suzuki-Miyaura coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Crystalline Porous Coordination Polymer Decorated with Nitroxyl
Radicals Catalyzes Aerobic Oxidation of Alcohols
