$DATUM N,N-Dimethyl-1-[3-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl]methanesulfonamide
(10a).
1-(3-Chloro-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl)-N,N-dimethylmethanesulfonamide
(1.44 g, 3.97 mmol),
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H pyrazole
(1.24 g, 5.95 mmol), tri-tert-butylphosphonium tetrafluoroborate (104 mg,
0.357 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (145 mg, 0.159 mmol), and potassium fluoride (761
mg, 13.1 mmol) were combined as solids and then placed under a nitrogen
atmosphere. DMF (39.7 mL) was added, and the resulting suspension was
heated to 130 °C and left to stir for 1 h. Then the reaction was cooled
to room temperature and partitioned between saturated aqueous sodium
hydrogen carbonate (250 mL) and dichloromethane (250 mL). The organic
layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica (EtOAc + 10% MeOH/hexanes gradient). Yield: (1.33 g, 3.25 mmol,
82%), yellow solid. 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 9.21 (d, 1H), 8.54 (d,
1H), 8.47 (s, 1H), 8.19 (s, 1H), 8.14 (s, 1H), 7.81 (m, 2H), 7.40 (d,
1H), 7.32 (d, 1H), 4.63 (s, 2H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 2.74 (s, 6H). MS (APCI)
calcd for C21H21N4O3S [M + H]+, 409.1; found, 409.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
1-[3-(1-Methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl]-N-(pyridin-2-ylmethyl)methanesulfonamide
(MK-8033): A Specific c-Met/Ron Dual Kinase Inhibitor with Preferential
Affinity for the Activated State of c-Met
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
