$DATUM 127-19-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. General procedure of Miyaura borylations
(at 1 mol% Pd loading). To an oven-dried Schlenk tube was charged aryl
bromide (aryl bromide or chloride was charged at the beginning unless it
was a liquid with a low boiling point, 1 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron
(1.5 mmol), potassium acetate (3 mmol), Bedford Pd precursor (5 μmol),
and ligand 5 (10 μmol). The Schlenk tube was pumped under vacuum and
refilled with nitrogen (this sequence was repeated for 3 times). To the
mixture was charged degassed N,N-dimethylacetamide (2 mL, aryl bromide
was also charged via syringe at this position if it was a liquid with a
low boiling point). The resulting mixture was heated to 100 °C and
stirred at this temperature under nitrogen for 12 h, and then cooled to
room temperature. To the mixture was added water (20 mL) and ethyl
acetate (20 mL). The ethyl acetate layer was separated, washed with water
(20 mL X 2) and brine, dried over sodium sulfate, concentrated, and
purifed by flash column chromatography (hexanes and ethyl acetate as
eluents) to provide the desired arylboronic ester.
3,5-Dimethyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)isoxazole:
colorless oil (82%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.46 (s, 3H), 2.28 (s,
3H), 1.26 (s, 12H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,CDCl3) δ 178.0, 164.3, 83.2, 25.1,
13.0, 11.9; EI-MS: m/z 223.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Muyaura borylation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Monophosphorus Ligands for Palladium-Catalyzed Miyaura
Borylation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
