$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Suzuki-Coupling Conditions. A solution
of dibromo compound 1a-d (1.00 eq) and
2-(5'-hexyl-2,2'-bithiophen-5-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
2 (3.00 eq) in a mixture of toluene/2 M aqueous Na2CO3 solution (4:1;
[dibromobenzotriazole] = 15 mM) and a few drops of Aliquat 336 was purged
with argon for about 1 h. Pd(PPh3)4 (~ 8 mol%) was added in one portion
and the mixture was refluxed until the starting material has been
consumed according to the TLC analysis. The reaction mixture was allowed
to cool to rt and diluted with MeOH to precipitate the desired product.
4,7-Bis(5'-hexyl-2,2'-bithiophen-5-yl)-2-(3,4,5-trifluorophenyl)-2H-benzotriazole
(3b): Following the general Suzuki-coupling conditions starting from
4,7-dibromo-2-(3,4,5-trifluorophenyl)-2H-benzotriazole (1b, 152 mg, 0.367
mmol) the reaction mixture was stirred 3 h at reflux temperature. After
precipitation with MeOH the solid residue was washed with H2O, MeOH,
acetone and pentane and then recrystallized from EtOAc/CHCl3 (1:1) to
yield the desired product as red needles (225 mg, 82%).
4,7-Bis(5'-hexyl-2,2'-bithiophen-5-yl)-2-(3,4,5-trifluorophenyl)-2H-benzotriazole
(3b), yield 225 mg, 82%. Mp = 187-189 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm
8.12 (dd, J = 8.11, 6.07 Hz, 2H), 7.96 (d, J = 3.85 Hz, 2H), 7.16 (d, J =
3.83 Hz, 2H), 7.09 (d, J = 3.51 Hz, 2H), 6.73 (dt, J = 3.54, 0.97 Hz,
2H), 2.88-2.79 (m, 4H), 1.73 (dt, J = 15.26, 7.45 Hz, 4H), 1.48-1.39 (m,
4H), 1.39-1.30 (m, 8H), 0.93-0.91 (m, 6H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ
ppm 151.71 (ddd, J = 250.90, 10.18, 4.26 Hz), 146.29, 143.28, 140.47 (dt,
J = 254.31, 15.37 Hz), 138.88, 137.49, 135.48, 134.82, 128.20, 125.12,
124.00 (t, J = 20.85 Hz), 123.56, 106.16-105.60 (m), 31.76, 31.75, 30.45,
29.89, 28.97, 22.75, 14.20. 19F NMR (471 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm -131.35 (d, J
= 20.49 Hz, 2F), -159.22 (t, J = 20.49 Hz, 1F). EI HRMS m/z (M+) calcd
for C40H38F3N3S4+: 745.1895; found 745.1879.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, quaternary ammonium compounds was used as catalyst
